Title: Signal Hill
Credit: Written by
Author: A. Writer
Draft date: November 2026

[[Written for Drafter for Claude's tests only (packages/mcp/test). Every line is original. It is not an in-app sample.]]

# Act One

INT. JUNE'S KITCHEN - NIGHT

= June hears a dead station come back to life.
[[Color: blue]]

A farmhouse kitchen. A shortwave set on the counter, older than the fridge. JUNE (71), reading glasses on a cord, turns the dial the way other people knit.

Static. Then a voice, warm and a little tinny.

ANNOUNCER (V.O.)
This is KSGH, Signal Hill, with the morning news for Thursday.

June freezes. She looks at the calendar on the wall. It is Wednesday.

JUNE
(to the radio)
You've been off the air since 1996.

ANNOUNCER (V.O.)
The Pruitt barn goes up at six-fifteen. No one is hurt.

She writes it on the back of an envelope. Her hand is steady. Her breathing isn't.

EXT. PRUITT FARM - DAWN

= The barn burns, exactly on time.
[[Color: red]]

ELI (16), hoodie, bike thrown in the ditch, stands at the fence with his phone up. June beside him in a coat over her nightgown.

The barn is quiet. Then it isn't. Smoke, then flame, all at once.

ELI
Gran. It's six-fifteen.

JUNE
I know what time it is.

ELI
How did you know?

JUNE
I didn't. The radio did.

Sirens in the distance. A cruiser crests the hill.

EXT. PRUITT FARM - CONTINUOUS

= The sheriff wants to know why they got here first.
[[Color: red]]

WES (50s), sheriff, hat in hand, walks over slowly. He has known June all his life and it shows in how carefully he speaks.

WES
June. You're up early.

JUNE
So's the barn.

WES
Eli called it in at six-oh-nine. Six minutes before it lit.

ELI
I can explain.

WES
Good. Somebody should.

[[Wes isn't hostile. He's scared, and he handles fear by being official.]]

INT. RAY'S WORKSHOP - DAY

= June asks the man who built the station what it could be.
[[Color: blue]]

Tubes, coils, a soldering iron in a coffee can. RAY (70s), the station's old engineer, doesn't look up from a radio in pieces.

RAY
The transmitter melted, June. I carried what was left of it out in a bucket.

JUNE
Then who's broadcasting?

RAY
Somebody with a sense of humour.

JUNE
It read the barn before it burned, Ray.

Ray sets the iron down. Finally looks at her.

RAY
Say that again. Slower.

# Act Two

EXT. SIGNAL HILL - DAY

= The ruin of the station, and a stranger already there.
[[Color: green]]

A bald hilltop. A concrete pad, a twisted mast lying in the grass like a dropped pencil. AMARA (30s), physicist, kneels beside a laptop wired to a coil of copper.

June, Eli, and Ray climb the last of the path.

AMARA
Don't step on the cable. Please.

ELI
Who are you?

AMARA
Amara. University. I've been picking up a carrier wave from this hill for three weeks.

RAY
There's nothing here to carry it.

AMARA
I noticed.

INT. AMARA'S VAN - NIGHT

= The signal arrives about eighteen hours early, every time.
[[Color: green]]

Equipment racked to the ceiling. Eli is wedged between a printer and a cooler. Amara points at a jagged line on a screen.

AMARA
Every broadcast lands about eighteen hours before the thing it describes.

ELI
So it's the future.

AMARA
It's a recording of the future. Those are different.

ELI
How?

AMARA
A recording can be wrong.

INT. SHERIFF'S OFFICE - DAY

= Wes is told the truth and doesn't like it.
[[Color: yellow]]

A small office, a big map of the county. Wes listens. June, Amara, and Eli sit in mismatched chairs.

WES
A radio that reads tomorrow's paper.

AMARA
Not the paper. A station. A specific one.

WES
KSGH burned when I was a deputy. I pulled Ray out of it myself.

JUNE
Then you know it didn't sign off properly.

Wes looks at the map for a long moment.

WES
What does it say about tomorrow?

INT. TOWN HALL - NIGHT

= Marcus sells the town a new tower on the hill.
[[Color: purple]]

Folding chairs, half full. MARCUS (40s), developer, good suit, easy smile, stands beside an easel with a drawing of a gleaming cell tower.

MARCUS
Signal Hill has been empty for thirty years. Let's give it something to do.

Polite applause. June, near the back, does not clap.

MARCUS (CONT'D)
Better coverage. Faster internet. Jobs.

JUNE
And the old foundation?

MARCUS
Gone by Friday.

Eli turns to her, alarmed. Friday is two days away.

INT. JUNE'S KITCHEN - LATER

= The radio reads a fire that hasn't happened yet: the hill.
[[Color: blue]]

The shortwave hisses. June, Eli, and Ray around the table, mugs going cold.

ANNOUNCER (V.O.)
Fire crews are at Signal Hill tonight, where the new construction site is lost.

RAY
That's not an accident. Nobody burns a site they're about to build on.

ELI
Unless they want the insurance.

JUNE
Or they want something on that hill gone for good.

[[This is the midpoint turn. Keep the three of them still; let the radio do the moving.]]

# Act Three

INT. MARCUS'S OFFICE - DAY

= Eli finds out what Marcus is really clearing.
[[Color: purple]]

Glass walls, a framed photograph of the old station. Eli waits by the desk, too polite to sit. Marcus comes in, distracted.

MARCUS
You're June's grandson.

ELI
Why do you have a picture of KSGH?

MARCUS
My father worked there. Nights.

ELI
Was he there when it burned?

Marcus takes the photograph down and puts it face first in a drawer.

MARCUS
Tell your grandmother the hearing is at nine.

EXT. SIGNAL HILL - NIGHT

= Everyone ends up on the hill at once.
[[Color: red]]

Wind. A bulldozer parked on the concrete pad. Amara's coil hums. June and Ray at the edge of the slab. Wes's headlights sweep across them.

A gas can tips over in the dark. Marcus stands beside it, empty-handed.

WES
Step away from that, Marcus.

MARCUS
I wasn't going to light it.

JUNE
The radio says you were.

MARCUS
Then the radio was wrong.

AMARA
(quietly)
A recording can be wrong.

INT. JUNE'S KITCHEN - DAWN

= The station reads one last bulletin: the one that didn't happen.
[[Color: blue]]

Grey light. Everyone crowded into the kitchen: June, Eli, Ray, Amara. Wes in the doorway. The shortwave crackles.

ANNOUNCER (V.O.)
Signal Hill is quiet this morning. No fire was reported.

A long silence. Ray laughs, once, surprised at himself.

RAY
It caught up.

ELI
With what?

JUNE
With us.

The voice says the date: today's. Then the static comes back, and stays.

EXT. SIGNAL HILL - DAY

= June stands where the station was, and lets it go.
[[Color: green]]

Sun on the concrete. The mast still in the grass. June alone, then Eli beside her.

ELI
Do you think it'll come back?

JUNE
I think it said what it needed to.

She takes the envelope from her coat, the one with the barn's time written on it, and lets the wind take it down the hill.

FADE OUT.
